<iscomment>
    Cartridge override of SFRA stock creditCardSummary.isml.
    The "Ending" and "/" literals live in the template, not the data, so the model-side
    fix that empties expirationMonth/Year when the masked PAN is missing would otherwise
    render "Ending /". Each line is gated on its own data so missing values suppress the
    whole line — same pattern as googlePaySummary.isml. Google Pay UC orders with no PAN/
    expiry render only the "Credit {type}" line.
</iscomment>
<div class="credit-card-type">
    <isif condition="${!empty(payment.type)}">
        <span>${Resource.msg('msg.payment.type.credit', 'confirmation', null)}
        ${payment.type}</span>
    </isif>
</div>
<div class="credit-card-number">
    <isif condition="${!empty(payment.maskedCreditCardNumber)}">
        <isprint value="${payment.maskedCreditCardNumber}" />
    </isif>
</div>
<div class="credit-card-expiration-date">
    <isif condition="${!empty(payment.expirationMonth) && !empty(payment.expirationYear)}">
        <span>${Resource.msg('msg.card.type.ending', 'confirmation', null)} ${payment.expirationMonth}/${payment.expirationYear}</span>
    </isif>
</div>
